    "text": "MECHANISM"
  },
  "documentClass": null,
  "metadata": {
    "uuid": "f5e0b97b-3647-4413-a16e-63dab2eaa40e"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00332:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00332:caption:fig-00001-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00332:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "Fatty acyl-coenzyme A reacts to form alpha, beta-unsaturated acyl-coenzyme A. This reacts with water to form beta hydroxyacyl-coenzyme A. This leads to beta-ketoacyl-coenzyme A which further forms acetyl-coenzyme A."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_29_03_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00006",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00332:title:sect-00006-title",
        "text": "Step 1 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Introduction of a Double Bond"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00001",
          "class": null,
          "title": null,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00002",
              "segmentId": "m00332:para:para-00002"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00002",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00332:alt:fig-00002-alt",
                  "text": "The oxidation of flavin adenine dinucleotide to flavin adenine dinucleotide dihydrogen. Flavin adenine dinucleotide contains flavin, ribitol, ribose, and adenine moieties."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_03_002.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00003",
              "segmentId": "m00332:para:para-00003"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00003",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00332:alt:fig-00003-alt",
                  "text": "Ribitol bonded acyl coenzyme A reacts to form a thioester enolate. This further leads to trans alpha, beta-unsaturated coenzyme A. Two hydrogen atoms in the reactant are labeled pro-R."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_03_003.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00004",
              "segmentId": "m00332:para:para-00004"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00004",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00332:alt:fig-00004-alt",
                  "text": "Flavin adenine dinucleotide reacts with coenzyme A via nucleophilic addition to form flavin adenine dinucleotide hydride and alpha-beta unsaturated coenzyme A. The reaction mechanism is depicted by arrows."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_03_004.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00002",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00332:title:sect-00002-title",
            "text": "Step 2 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Conjugate Addition of Water"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00005",
              "segmentId": "m00332:para:para-00005"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00005",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00332:alt:fig-00005-alt",
                  "text": "Acyl coenzyme A reacts with water and base to form an enolate intermediate. Protonation provides (3 S)-hydroxyacyl coenzyme A, with a  hydrogen and carbon labeled pro-R and S, respectively."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_03_005.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00003",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00332:title:sect-00003-title",
            "text": "Step 3 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Alcohol Oxidation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00006",
              "segmentId": "m00332:para:para-00006"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00006",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00332:alt:fig-00006-alt",
                  "text": "Enzyme reacts with beta-hydroxyacyl coenzyme A and nicotinamide dinucleotide cation to form nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide hydride, and beta ketoacyl coenzyme A. The reaction mechanism is depicted by arrows."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_03_006.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00004",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00332:title:sect-00004-title",
            "text": "Step 4 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Chain Cleavage"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00007",
              "segmentId": "m00332:para:para-00007"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00007",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00332:alt:fig-00007-alt",
                  "text": "A reversible reaction in which two esters react via Claisen reaction to form beta keto ester and other products. The beta keto ester undergoes retro claisen to form the esters."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_03_007.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00008",
              "segmentId": "m00332:para:para-00008"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00008",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00332:alt:fig-00008-alt",
                  "text": "An enzyme base reacts with beta-ketoacyl-coenzyme A to form an alkoxide ion intermediate that expels acetyl CoA and another intermediate that leads to chain-shortened acyl-coenzyme A."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_03_008.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00009",
              "segmentId": "m00332:para:para-00009"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00009",
              "class": "scaled-down",
              "caption": {
                "segmentId": "m00332:caption:fig-00009-caption"
              },
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00332:alt:fig-00009-alt",
                  "text": "Myristoyl-coenzyme A  is converted via beta-oxidation to lauroyl-coenzyme A, further beta-oxidation provided caproyl-coenzyme A, which undergoes a final beta-oxidation to form capryloyl-coenzyme A."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_03_009.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00010",
              "segmentId": "m00332:para:para-00010"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
